    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **69 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the welcome-notification requirement on successful owner creation.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `NotifyOwnerWelcome.java`:\n- Modeled on the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` step.\n- Logs via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\")` a line containing the owner id and memberId: `Welcome notification: id={} memberId={}`.\n- Reads the saved `Owner` via `@Val`, so it runs after the id and memberId are assigned.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted a `notifyWelcome` step (under `transaction` governance, consistent with neighboring steps) between `audit` and `respond`, so the notification is emitted only on the successful create path (the idempotent-replay branch short-circuits earlier via `respondExisting`).\n\nThe new `Cp57Tests.coreEnqueuesWelcome` asserts a NOTIFY log line contains both the owner id and the memberId \u2014 it passes, and all 69 tests remain green.",
